Pursuant to the authority vested in the undersigned and in accordance with the organization's established governance framework, the internal audit function is hereby directed to undertake, with all due diligence, an aggregation analysis encompassing the totality of control deficiencies identified during the current quarter's testing of Internal Control over Financial Reporting (ICFR).

WHEREAS individual control deficiencies have been identified that, severally, may not rise to the threshold of a material weakness, and WHEREAS it is incumbent upon the organization to determine whether such deficiencies, when considered in the aggregate, may collectively constitute a material weakness with respect to the same significant financial statement account balances or disclosures;

NOW, THEREFORE, the internal audit team is hereby instructed to perform the following:

(i) For each cluster of related deficiencies pertaining to the same significant account balance or disclosure, the team shall evaluate the likelihood that a misstatement could occur, giving due consideration to the nature of the controls implicated therein and the existence vel non of compensating controls that may mitigate the risk attendant thereto;

(ii) The team shall further evaluate the magnitude of potential misstatement by examining, inter alia, the financial statement amounts and transaction volumes exposed to each such deficiency;

(iii) The scope of said analysis shall encompass all significant accounts and relevant assertions tested pursuant to AS 2201, without limitation or exception;

(iv) The findings and conclusions of the foregoing analysis shall be memorialized and documented in a format deemed suitable for presentation to, and discussion with, the organization's external auditors in connection with the upcoming interim review;

(v) The preliminary results of said analysis shall be prepared and made available for the Audit Committee's review no later than the end of next week, time being of the essence;

(vi) Any combinations of deficiencies that, in the professional judgment of the internal audit team, warrant escalation as potential material weaknesses shall be expressly flagged and brought to the immediate attention of the appropriate parties.

The undersigned hereby reserves the right to request supplementary analysis or clarification as may be deemed necessary upon review of the preliminary findings. Failure to comply with the foregoing directives within the stipulated timeframe shall be considered a matter of material concern.

Pursuant to the organizational mandate and in accordance with established information security governance frameworks, the undersigned hereby requests that the assessment plan pertaining to the forthcoming penetration test of the corporate network infrastructure be brought to final disposition no later than close of business Friday, said deadline being non-negotiable and binding upon all parties responsible for deliverable completion.

WHEREAS the scope of said engagement shall encompass all systems residing upon the 10.20.0.0/16 subnet, comprising approximately 340 hosts distributed across the primary data center and two (2) regional office facilities;

BE IT RESOLVED that the aforementioned plan shall explicitly enumerate, in exhaustive fashion, all authorized IP ranges within scope, and shall further delineate, with specificity, any and all systems expressly excluded from testing activities. It is hereby stipulated that the exclusion list shall include, at minimum and without limitation: (a) the payroll database designated as PAYDB-PROD, residing at 10.20.44.12, and (b) the legacy SCADA gateway system;

FURTHERMORE, the undersigned directs that the plan shall incorporate within its scope the forty-five (45) systems hosted upon the network infrastructure of Meridian DataServices pursuant to the existing managed hosting agreement between the parties. The undersigned acknowledges and notes for the record that written consent from Meridian DataServices authorizing testing activities upon their infrastructure has not yet been obtained as of the date hereof; notwithstanding the foregoing, the plan shall reflect full and complete coverage of said hosts, with the understanding and express stipulation that authorization shall be pursued and secured in parallel with plan finalization. The assessment is hereby directed to commence Monday morning;

THE UNDERSIGNED FURTHER REQUESTS the drafting of a short authorization memorandum, not to exceed one (1) to two (2) pages in length, which memorandum shall serve as documentary proof that assessors presenting themselves on-site to system owners or end users are duly sanctioned and authorized to conduct the testing activities described herein;

IN ADDITION THERETO, the plan shall address and provide provisions for: (i) incident handling procedures to be invoked in the event that adverse or unintended consequences arise during the course of testing; (ii) protocols governing the handling, storage, and disposition of sensitive data encountered during the engagement; and (iii) logistical considerations including, but not limited to, team composition and designated communication channels;

The responsible parties are hereby directed to exercise best efforts to render the overall plan as thorough and comprehensive as reasonably practicable, while maintaining sufficient conciseness to facilitate executive-level review and approval.

Pursuant to the organizational mandate requiring periodic evaluation of information security infrastructure, the undersigned hereby requests a comprehensive assessment and formal documentation of the current log management architecture, benchmarked against the guidance set forth in NIST SP 800-92, with particular emphasis on our second-tier architecture.

WHEREAS the enterprise presently maintains a single centralized log server tasked with the collection, analysis, and both short-term and long-term storage of log data across the entirety of the organizational domain; and

WHEREAS leadership has expressed a material interest in understanding the risk posture attendant to said configuration;

NOW THEREFORE, the designated analyst or analysts shall undertake the following:

1. Evaluate whether the aforementioned single-server approach constitutes a reasonably appropriate architectural disposition given the organization's size and operational footprint, and render a professional opinion thereon.

2. Produce a written gap analysis ("the Deliverable") that shall address, without limitation, the following matters:

   a. The presence or absence of redundancy capabilities within the current infrastructure;

   b. The adequacy of failover arrangements available to log generators in the event that the primary server becomes unavailable or otherwise ceases to function;

   c. Whether it would be advisable and prudent to transition to a multi-server topology incorporating specialized functional separation, including but not limited to the segregation of collection and analysis functions from long-term storage responsibilities;

   d. Whether the existing infrastructure provides for log data sharing between servers for the purposes of redundancy and continuity of operations.

3. Include within the Deliverable any and all recommendations for architectural modifications deemed necessary or advisable, and further identify and flag any scalability concerns that may bear upon the organization's future operational requirements.

The Deliverable shall be transmitted to the SOC leadership team no later than end of next week, such that the findings contained therein may be duly incorporated into the quarterly infrastructure review then pending.

The undersigned reserves the right to request supplemental analysis or clarification as may be warranted upon receipt and review of said Deliverable.

Pursuant to the organizational mandate governing incident response documentation standards, the undersigned hereby requests the development and formalization of a comprehensive final incident report template, said template to be aligned in all material respects with the NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 2 incident handling lifecycle framework, for deployment and uniform adoption across all Security Operations Center (SOC) teams operating under the organization's purview.

The aforementioned template shall, in its entirety, address and encompass the full incident response process, commencing from initial detection and progressing through post-incident activity, inclusive of but not limited to an executive summary section. Said executive summary shall articulate, in language accessible to non-technical leadership and requiring no specialized technical background for comprehension, the nature of the incident as it occurred, and shall further set forth how formal incident response capabilities aided—or, in the alternative, would have aided—in the mitigation of risk and the expeditious limitation of damage.

The template shall furthermore incorporate, without limitation, the following provisions:

(i) Dedicated sections for the thorough documentation of all affected data, applications, and services implicated in the incident;

(ii) A formal confirmation mechanism attesting that all impacted systems have been restored to normal operational status;

(iii) A structured and chronologically ordered timeline of all response actions undertaken during the course of the incident;

(iv) Full support for the updated attack vector categories as enumerated in the current revision of the governing standard;

(v) Integration of the expanded incident metrics list for the purpose of measuring and evaluating response effectiveness;

(vi) Designated fields for the identification of attacking hosts, it being expressly noted that the focus shall be directed toward host identification rather than attacker attribution;

(vii) A report format that shall facilitate and enable information sharing with external parties, including but not limited to US-CERT and ISACs, in a manner consistent with the organization's coordination obligations as currently established.

The undersigned respectfully directs that a draft of said template be prepared and made available for review by the incident response team leads by end of next week, such that the template may be piloted during the upcoming tabletop exercise.

All parties are hereby advised to govern themselves accordingly.

Pursuant to the foregoing and in accordance with the professional obligations incumbent upon the engagement team, the undersigned hereby requests and directs the preparation of a comprehensive risk assessment workpaper, said workpaper to encompass, without limitation, the totality of financial relationships and transactions subsisting between the entity under audit and its executive officers, in full conformity with the requirements set forth under AS 2110.

WHEREAS the interim fieldwork deadline falls on Friday next, the engagement team shall ensure timely delivery of the aforementioned deliverable on or before said date;

NOW THEREFORE, the workpaper shall document, inter alia, the following procedures undertaken by the engagement team:

(i) A thorough reading and substantive analysis of all employment agreements and compensation contracts pertaining to current executive officers of the audited entity;

(ii) A comprehensive review of all proxy statement disclosures made by or on behalf of the entity;

(iii) An examination of any and all other relevant SEC filings or regulatory submissions bearing upon executive compensation arrangements, including but not limited to perquisites, side agreements, and ancillary benefits of any nature whatsoever.

FURTHERMORE, the undersigned hereby instructs the engagement team to exercise best professional judgment in identifying such additional procedures as may be deemed appropriate given the particular facts and circumstances of the client entity. The undersigned emphasizes that said supplemental procedures shall be "exhaustive and complete" in scope, such that the firm may affirmatively demonstrate that no avenue of inquiry has been left unexplored.

BE IT FURTHER NOTED that each financial relationship or transaction so identified shall be mapped, with specificity, to the corresponding risks of material misstatement at both the financial statement level and the relevant assertion level.

WHEREAS the client entity disclosed, as recently as yesterday, two (2) new executive employment agreements incorporating complex multi-year clawback provisions and deferred compensation arrangements, the engagement team is hereby directed to incorporate a full and complete analysis of said agreements into the workpaper, notwithstanding the additional burden thereby imposed, and without prejudice to the Friday deadline, which shall remain in full force and effect.

The foregoing constitutes the full scope of the request, and compliance therewith is expected in all material respects.

**MEMORANDUM**

**RE: Privacy Program Plan Alignment Review — Annual Financial Reporting Package**

Pursuant to the organizational mandate governing year-end financial close procedures, the undersigned hereby requests that the assembled team undertake and complete the following obligations in a timely and thorough manner.

WHEREAS the organization is presently engaged in the preparation of its year-end financial reporting package, and WHEREAS it is incumbent upon all responsible parties to ensure that privacy program documentation maintains full conformity with the Risk Management Framework requirements as set forth in NIST SP 800-37 Rev. 2;

NOW THEREFORE, the undersigned directs that a duly qualified member or members of the team shall be designated to conduct a comprehensive review of the current privacy program plan, said review to verify and confirm, without limitation, the following:

(a) That the privacy program plan adequately and sufficiently describes the organizational structure of the privacy program in its entirety;

(b) That the strategic goals and objectives therein are articulated with reasonable specificity;

(c) That the role, responsibilities, and authorities of the Senior Agency Official for Privacy, together with all supporting staff, are delineated in accordance with applicable requirements;

(d) That program management controls and common controls—whether currently in place or planned for future implementation—are documented with sufficient particularity;

FURTHERMORE, the reviewing party or parties shall confirm that the privacy posture assessment, as currently constituted, accurately and faithfully reflects the status of the organization's information systems and information resources—including but not limited to personnel, equipment, funds, and IT assets—and that the organization can affirmatively demonstrate the capabilities necessary to comply with all applicable privacy requirements and obligations.

The reviewing party shall, upon identification of any deficiencies, map all gaps between the current documentation and the framework requirements as stipulated herein, and shall prepare and deliver a remediation roadmap setting forth recommended corrective actions with appropriate prioritization.

BE IT NOTED that the entirety of the foregoing review shall be concluded and all deliverables furnished prior to the commencement of fieldwork by the external auditors next month. Time is of the essence.

It is further stipulated that the scope of said review shall encompass system security and privacy plans to confirm that said plans detail the implementation methodologies for controls with adequate specificity. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the undersigned hereby delegates to the team the discretion to determine appropriate scope boundaries with respect to which systems and environments of operation shall be included within the ambit of this review, provided such determination is made in good faith and with due regard for materiality and risk.

This directive shall be effective immediately upon distribution.
